# Build context for the API image (Dockerfile.api, context = repo root).
# A local node_modules in the build context breaks `pnpm install` in the
# image build: pnpm tries to purge the copied modules directory and aborts
# with ERR_PNPM_ABORTED_REMOVE_MODULES_DIR_NO_TTY (no TTY in ACR builds).
# This happened on the S-B8 deploy (Nov 13, 2026) when the Cloud Shell clone
# had accumulated a 1.3 GB node_modules from the web build's pnpm install.
# The build reinstalls everything from the lockfile, so excluding the local
# tree is safe — and it keeps the 1.3 GB out of the uploaded context.
node_modules
.git
# A local .env must never be copied into the image: it holds provider keys
# and tokens. No .env file is tracked today (only .env.example, a template),
# but a clone that picked one up would otherwise ship its secrets in the
# build context — the same way a stray node_modules once broke the build.
.env*
